Yes. We should rebuild it cleanly rather than keep modifying the first prototype.

For the Agent interface, I’d structure the workflow as four states: Dashboard → À traiter → Traitement en cours → Historique. The agent never imports anything and never chooses another agent. Their page is strictly for processing assigned lines.

Before the Manager is connected, we’ll keep one realistic test record in JavaScript. Later, we replace only the data-loading part; the Agent UI/workflow won’t need to be rewritten.

